  {
   "id": "fdm-knockdown",
   "kind": "core",
   "title": "FDM inter-layer knock-down: tension along z of a bar with inter-layer factor 0.6 and yield 250 MPa",
   "reference": "Definition used by the package (docs/EXTENSIONS_SPEC.md section 4, A3): tension across the printed layers is divided by the inter-layer factor before it is compared with the yield strength. The bar carries 100 MPa along z, so the safety factor is yield / sigma = 2.5 when the layers lie along x or y (the load is in the layers), and f yield / sigma = 1.5 when the layers stack along z (print axis z, the load pulls the layers apart); with the knock-down switched off it is 2.5 in both. An exact consequence of the definition, not a measurement of any material: it checks the code, not the factor.",
   "setup": {
    "features": [
     {
      "type": "box",
      "body": "Bar",
      "size": [
       10,
       10,
       80
      ],
      "anchor": "min",
      "pos": [
       0,
       0,
       0
      ]
     }
    ],
    "customMaterials": [
