   "title": "Bolt preload of 1 000 N through discs of radius 5 mm on the two faces of the block",
   "reference": "Equilibrium (exact): the two discs push toward each other with 1000 N, so every cross-section between them carries a compressive force of 1000 N. The sliders only hold normal displacements, so they have no z reaction in the upper half and the part above the mid plane is held in equilibrium by 1000 N from the part below: the element nodal forces on the plane nodes sum to 1000 N (weak-form equilibrium, exact up to the solver tolerance), and the sum of the element-centre sigma_zz h^2 over the slab above the plane agrees with -1000 N within 3 %. A first version of this case used a fixed wall instead of sliders and read 7.9 % low: the wall carried local reactions of both signs (zero net), so the section force through the upper half was not the preload; the case was redesigned, not its tolerance.",
